msgstr ""

#: events-certificates.php:33
msgid "Events Certificates: the PDF and QR code libraries are missing. In the plugin folder, run bin/install.sh (see .github/CONTRIBUTING.md)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:63
msgid "Attendance certificates anyone can verify by code: events, their participants (registered, attended, no-show) and the certificates of who attended."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:126
msgid "How many per page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:132
msgid "Page number, from 1."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:197
msgid "The event's name, as certificates show it, e.g. \"WordPress Meetup: Blocks in practice\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:202
msgid "When it starts, \"YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM\" in the site's time zone (see get-overview)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:207
msgid "When it ends, \"YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM\" in the site's time zone. Defaults to the start."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:211
msgid "Where it happens, e.g. \"Recife, PE\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:215
msgid "The community or group that holds it, e.g. \"WordPress Curitiba\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:219
msgid "The venue, e.g. \"Community Hall\". With the city it makes the place the certificates show."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:223
msgid "The city, e.g. \"Curitiba, PR\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:227
msgid "The speakers, as they go on the certificates (optional)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:232
msgid "Show the workload (from start to end) on the certificates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:237
msgid "The event's page (Meetup, GatherPress…)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:243
msgid "Workload in hours on the certificates. Omit to count from start to end."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:252
msgid "Workload in hours by role (attendee, speaker, organizer, volunteer, sponsor): an organizer's 40, a volunteer's 8. A role left out uses the event's hours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:256
msgid "Who signs this event's certificates. Omit to use the site's signer (get-settings)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:260
msgid "The signer's role, e.g. \"Meetup organizer\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:530
msgid "People to add. The same person (same e-mail, or same name) is updated, not added twice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:539
msgid "The name exactly as it goes on the certificate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:547
msgid "attendee, speaker, organizer, volunteer or sponsor (or their translated names); several with / or +. Templates are chosen by role."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:552
msgid "Several roles of the same person, each with its own certificate: a speaker who is also an organizer. A person already on the list gains them, never loses one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:557
msgid "registered (default), attended or no_show. Only attended ones get certificates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:561
msgid "WordPress.org username, for the avatar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:569
msgid "Or CSV text, such as Meetup's \"Attendee details\" export: a \"Name\" column (and optionally \"Email\"); RSVP \"No\" rows are left out and rows marked absent come in as no_show. Up to 5 MB."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:582
msgid "Give the \"event_id\": see events-certificates/get-events."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:586
msgid "There is no such event: see events-certificates/get-events."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:650
msgid "The event's ID (events-certificates/get-events)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:659
msgid "Participant IDs (events-certificates/get-participants)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:665
msgid "Get certificates overview"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:666
msgid "Start here. Says whether certificates can be verified on this site (a public address) and where; who signs; how many certificates exist by status; the events and templates; the integrations active (GatherPress, CampTix); the site's time zone for event times; and the usual order of the other abilities."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:679
msgid "Get events"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:680
msgid "Lists the events certificates are issued for, newest first, with their dates, place, signer and how many participants registered, attended, didn't come and got certificates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:689
msgid "Words in the event's name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:711
msgid "Get participants"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:712
msgid "Lists an event's participants with their status (registered, attended, no_show) and certificate, if any (code, verification and PDF addresses). Filter by status, or \"certified\" for those with a certificate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:726
msgid "Part of a name or e-mail."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:748
msgid "Get certificates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:749
msgid "Lists or searches certificates (by name, e-mail or code), of every event or one, with their verification page and PDF addresses. Also answers \"is this code valid?\": search the code and read its status."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:758
msgid "Part of a name, e-mail or code."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:763
msgid "issued (valid), replaced (corrected by a newer one) or revoked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:768
msgid "Only this event's certificates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:772
msgid "Only the certificates of this role (attendee, speaker, organizer, volunteer, sponsor)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:804
msgid "Create event"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:805
msgid "Adds an event to issue certificates for. Then add its participants (events-certificates/add-participants). For a list of people who all came, events-certificates/quick-issue does everything at once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:823
msgid "Update event"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:824
msgid "Changes an event's name, dates, place, link, hours or signer; only the fields given change. Its certificates show the new name, place, dates and signer at once (the people's names and hours stay as issued)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:842
#: includes/events-admin.php:231
#: includes/events-admin.php:1149
#: includes/events-admin.php:1325
#: includes/events-admin.php:1394
msgid "Add participants"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:843
msgid "Adds people to an event, as a list and/or CSV text (such as a Meetup attendee export). Someone already on the list is updated, not added again. Says how many were added, updated, left out for RSVP \"No\" and came in as no-shows."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:854
msgid "Mark everyone given as attended (unless the CSV says absent or a person has a status)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:878
msgid "Set participant status"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:879
msgid "Marks participants of an event as attended (check-in), no_show or registered. Certificates already issued stay valid; revoke one with events-certificates/revoke-certificate."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:910
msgid "Remove participants"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:911
msgid "Moves people to the event's Trash, out of its list (they can be restored in the admin). Their certificates, if issued, stay valid (revoke them separately)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:937
#: includes/class-all-people-list-table.php:67
#: includes/class-people-list-table.php:262
msgid "Issue certificates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:938
msgid "Issues the certificates of an event's participants who attended: the ones given, or everyone who attended; one certificate for each role of each person (or of the roles given). Someone who already has one keeps it (same code); a revoked one is not issued again. Returns each certificate with its code, verification page and PDF address."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:953
msgid "Only these participants; omit for everyone who attended."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:959
msgid "Only the certificates of these roles; omit for every role of each participant (one certificate per role)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:990
msgid "Revoke certificate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:991
msgid "Revokes a certificate: its page then says it was revoked, with the reason. It can't be undone; issue a new one if needed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1001
msgid "The certificate code, XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1006
msgid "Shown on the certificate's page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1020
msgid "Quick issue"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1021
msgid "Creates an event, adds who attended (a list and/or CSV text such as a Meetup export) and issues their certificates, in one step. Everyone given counts as attended unless they have a status or the CSV marks them absent. Returns the event and the certificates with their addresses. Running it again creates another event."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1048
msgid "Get certificate settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1049
msgid "The settings: who signs (name, role, whether a signature is set), the place shown when an event has none, the date certificates show as issued, and whether the site is treated as public."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1062
msgid "Update certificate settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1063
msgid "Changes the settings given: who signs (name, role, a signature as SVG code with filled paths), the default place, the date of issue, and whether the site is treated as public. Every certificate shows the change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1073
msgid "SVG code of the signature; only filled paths are kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1080
msgid "issued: the day each certificate was issued; event_end: the event's last day."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1084
msgid "Treat the site as public (prints QR codes and codes). Only for a staging site anyone can open."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1088
msgid "Print a code and a QR code on the certificates so anyone can check them (needs a public site). Off by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1092
msgid "Offer attendees the declaration page (a second page with the days and talks declared and, if you ask for it, an identification document). Off by default."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1096
msgid "The country (ISO code, like BR) whose identification document the declaration page asks for: the CPF for Brazil. One, or empty for none (the default)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1100
msgid "Let attendees say they are not from that country (“Sou estrangeiro”): they give a passport instead, or nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1115
msgid "Import WordCamp people"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1116
msgid "Imports into an event the speakers, organizers and volunteers this WordCamp site keeps (wc-post-types): they come in as attended, each with their role; someone with two roles is one person with both, and importing again adds roles, never removes. Then issue certificates with events-certificates/issue-certificates (one per role)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1145
msgid "Import GatherPress event"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1146
msgid "Imports a GatherPress event and its RSVPs (or syncs it again): \"attending\" ones come in as registered, checked-in ones as attended; waiting list and \"not attending\" stay out; nobody is demoted. Then issue certificates with events-certificates/issue-certificates. GatherPress event IDs are its gatherpress_event posts."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1232
msgid "To certify an event: events-certificates/create-event, then add-participants (a list or a Meetup CSV), set-participant-status to \"attended\" for who came, and issue-certificates; or quick-issue for all at once. get-certificates lists codes with their verification and PDF addresses. When \"verifiable\" is false the site is not public, so certificates carry no QR code or code."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1412
msgid "Give \"participants\" (a list of names) or \"csv\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1448
msgid "The \"status\" must be registered, attended or no_show."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1451
#: includes/abilities.php:1473
msgid "Give the \"participant_ids\": see events-certificates/get-participants."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1523
msgid "Give the certificate \"code\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1527
msgid "There is no certificate with that code: see events-certificates/get-certificates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1530
msgid "Only a valid certificate can be revoked: this one was already replaced or revoked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1601
#: includes/admin.php:342
msgid "The signature was not saved: paste the code of an SVG file with filled paths."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1645
msgid "Give the \"gatherpress_event_id\"."
msgstr ""

